  <title>4.4.2: Defining Functions by a Rule</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00900</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.2: Defining Functions by a Rule</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d84fafab-22a6-4e68-be4a-2f0dc7c35571</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>For 1 - 4, match each equation with a verbal description that represents the same function. </para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="c23b5406-28c3-4e37-83da-b47375a3e5ae" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="32e60369-cf54-4d64-98aa-ddb3caaf2b97" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result." data-solution-options="[&quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;, &quot;Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(f(x)=3x−7\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  
  
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e77644a4-d0b5-4b56-8fe5-91718aca8f88" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3." data-solution-options="[&quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;, &quot;Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(g(x) =3(x−7)\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  
  
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d0caed67-e03b-43d8-a279-1893700d4ee1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result." data-solution-options="[&quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;, &quot;Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(h(x)\;=\;\frac x3-7\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  </div>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  
  
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3afd615d-65d5-4183-9c36-f828395b7160" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3." data-solution-options="[&quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;, &quot;Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(h(x)\;=\;\frac{x-7}{3}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="solution" data-content-id="63b1bc11-5409-4479-9553-a029964c23d0" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
    <!--pulldown-->
    <exercise data-content-id="d4ff6a33-3678-47ae-8089-254e858309ff" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="\(g\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(k\\)&quot;]">
      <problem>
        <para>For one of the functions, when the input is 6, the output is –3. Which is that function: \(f\), \(g\), \(h\), or \(k\)? </para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>
  </div>
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->


<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain how you knew the answer to question 5.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers: Your answers may vary. </para>
    <para>The correct answer is \(k(x)\). When x is 0, \(k(x)\) has the greatest value because \(k(0) = \frac{0 - 7}{3} = - \frac{7}{3} = -2 \frac13\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="solution" data-content-id="1000f1b2-03ab-4e77-9f11-42f389a7e4d9" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--pulldown-->
  <exercise data-content-id="834a1a5b-36c8-4d51-889f-2ed2f0303ef2" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="\(k\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(k\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which function value, \(f\), \(g\), \(h\), or \(k\) is the greatest when the input is 0.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>When \(x\) is 0, \(k(x)\) has the greatest value.
      </para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="16aa1a9d-afa6-49df-ada7-e03acaa1f2c1" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="\(f\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(k\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which function value, \(f\), \(g\), \(h\), or \(k\) is the greatest when the input is 10.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)\). When x is 10, \(f(10) = 3(10) - 7 = 30 -7 = 23\) and, 23 is larger than \(g(10) = 9, h(10) = - \frac{11}{3}\), and \(k(10) = 1\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
</div>
<!--Interaction End -->


